{
  "requirement": "`habeas::validate()` MUST check the current Cargo and mdBook project and make its Cargo test fail with all validation errors when any requirement evidence is invalid.\nIts failure message MUST instruct the agent to run `habeas author --all`, address\nthe reported gaps, and rerun tests. Validation MUST remain deterministic and MUST\nNOT invoke authoring itself. {cite}`requirements.authoring.batch`\n{cite}`requirements.authoring.deterministic_validation`",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Implementation.** `habeas::validate()` in `src/lib.rs` (lines 29–52) carries the `{impl}` marker for `requirements.integration.validate`. It meets each obligation:\n- **Finds the project.** It walks up from the current directory to the nearest ancestor containing both `Cargo.toml` and `book.toml`. It panics if none exists, so the Cargo test fails.\n- **Reports all errors.** It calls `validate_repository(root)`, which runs the full ordinary inspection. If `report.errors` is non-empty, it panics with the counts and every error joined together.\n- **Instructs the agent.** The panic message says \"Run `habeas author --all` to author missing or outdated evidence … then address any reported gaps and rerun the tests.\"\n- **Never authors.** `validate()` and `validate_repository` call nothing from the authoring path. `src/evidence.rs` (around line 259) carries a comment and an `{impl}` marker for `requirements.authoring.deterministic_validation`, and reports missing evidence as an error instead of starting authoring.\n\nThe panic message adds one extra sentence (\"Do not write evidence judgments or snapshots by hand.\"). It is guidance consistent with the requirement and does not change behaviour. The inspection code that `validate()` calls is implemented under other requirements, such as `report_api` and the `ci.*` requirements. The two cited requirements, `authoring.batch` and `authoring.deterministic_validation`, are context here and were not reassessed.\n\n**Tests.** `tests/validate.rs` runs `habeas::validate()` in a child test process, so it can observe a real test failure:\n- `validate_fails_the_test_with_every_error_and_authoring_instructions` builds a fixture with one requirement lacking evidence and one malformed evidence file. It starts from a nested directory, so it also covers the project-root search. It asserts:\n  - the process fails;\n  - the output contains both errors (`rules.ready` and `evidence/rules.broken.json`);\n  - the output contains the `habeas author --all` and \"address any reported gaps and rerun the tests\" instructions;\n  - no evidence file or Habeas state is written, so validation does not author;\n  - a repeat run gives the same error lines, so validation is deterministic;\n  - valid evidence makes the test pass.\n- `validate_fails_outside_a_cargo_and_mdbook_project` covers the failure case where no `book.toml` exists. It asserts the \"cannot find Cargo and mdBook project root\" message.\n\nThe tests cover the main points: multiple errors reported together, the message text, no authoring and no side effects, determinism, success, and the missing-project failure. The only untested path is `validate_repository` returning an I/O error. That is an unlikely edge, and it is not part of the stated requirement. There are no FIXME markers or acknowledged gaps.",
  "references": "3e2ad8f756389f4b1c51ff653bc033c4b252c9d1745ee052b4c508e81e20cb8c",
  "inputs": [
